reply.body:
@luigidellaquila I see there is a mention of double backtick escaping on [`master` docs branch](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/master/esql-syntax.html#esql-identifiers)

> When referencing a function alias that itself uses a quoted identifier, the backticks of the quoted identifier need to be escaped with another backtick.

Let me know if need to add to this.

timeline.body:
The changes in the PR LGTM.

**But**, to save us time, a bug report, a new PR and a round of reviews, the `enrich` command needs an update as well. And we could do it in this PR.

`ExpressionBuilder.enrichFieldName` method should be changed to (and some tests added, maybe `ROW a = \"1\" | ENRICH languages_policy ON a WITH ```name``*` = language_name`):

```
    private NamedExpression enrichFieldName(EsqlBaseParser.QualifiedNamePatternContext ctx) {
        var name = visitQualifiedNamePattern(ctx);
        if (name != null && name instanceof UnresolvedNamePattern up) {
            throw new ParsingException(source(ctx), "Using wildcards (*) in ENRICH WITH projections is not allowed [{}]", up.pattern());
        }
        return name;
    }
```

